WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.126
Wall Street wiped about two

00:00:01.926 --> 00:00:04.166
point three trillion dollars off

00:00:03.966 --> 00:00:05.697
AI stocks in a single day.

00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:07.273
The trigger was voters.

00:00:07.973 --> 00:00:09.642
The Nasdaq 100 fell six

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.729
point three percent on Thursday.

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:13.072
Two days earlier,

00:00:12.872 --> 00:00:15.018
midterm voters turned hard against

00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:15.732
data centers.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.915
The closer to the hardware,

00:00:17.715 --> 00:00:18.373
the worse.

00:00:18.413 --> 00:00:19.968
The Dow lost three point

00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:21.933
four percent, Nvidia nine point

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:23.355
two, and the chip index

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:24.439
twelve point three.

00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:27.828
Voters faced forty-one local measures

00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:29.148
on data centers,

00:00:28.948 --> 00:00:30.138
by CNBC's count.

00:00:30.178 --> 00:00:32.272
They sided against data centers

00:00:32.072 --> 00:00:33.043
in all but one.

00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:35.666
Governors-elect in Texas,

00:00:35.466 --> 00:00:37.538
Georgia and Ohio back pauses

00:00:37.338 --> 00:00:39.489
or limits on new construction.

00:00:39.529 --> 00:00:41.277
The common thread is anger

00:00:41.077 --> 00:00:42.262
over power bills.

00:00:42.812 --> 00:00:44.522
The seven biggest US tech

00:00:44.322 --> 00:00:46.249
companies lost more than one

00:00:46.049 --> 00:00:47.328
trillion dollars.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:48.979
Cloud giants fell less,

00:00:48.779 --> 00:00:50.647
because their data centers are

00:00:50.447 --> 00:00:51.417
already built.

00:00:51.457 --> 00:00:53.773
Chipmakers sell into buildings that

00:00:53.573 --> 00:00:54.660
do not exist yet.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.267
Your A P I bill

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.553
will not change tomorrow.

00:00:57.593 --> 00:00:59.477
Watch G P U rental

00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:01.655
prices in 2027 and 2028,

00:01:01.455 --> 00:01:04.230
where your provider builds,

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.517
and efficiency.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.089
Campaign promises are not law.

00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:09.742
The real signal is what

00:01:09.542 --> 00:01:11.528
the new governors sign after

00:01:11.328 --> 00:01:13.388
taking office early next year.

00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:15.583
One analyst called it an

00:01:15.383 --> 00:01:17.317
AI bubble losing some air,

00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:18.039
not a burst.

00:01:18.079 --> 00:01:19.724
Either way, the hard part

00:01:19.524 --> 00:01:21.420
now looks like permits and power.

